{
  "design_rationale": "First-order heat-loss model y_ss=amb+K*u with amb~0.175 K~1.1 from E5 settled 0.505 at u=0.3, E2 ambient ~0.175 at u=0, E1/E8 consistent. Tau ~150-250s (still rising after 250-360s, settled after ~540s) so closed-loop Tc~90s via Kp=0.9 gives settling <300s. Feedforward u_ff=(target-amb)/K gives correct bias ~0.296 for 0.5; P halves residual FF error, I trims rest. I gated to |e|<0.15 and limited to +-0.20 in u (int_lim 25 with Ki=0.008) to prevent windup during 0.32 initial error while leaving authority for >0.1 FF error. EMA tau_f=12s smooths +-0.02 noise; single-sample dips -0.05 to -0.07 rejected by -0.04/+0.06 outlier gate with 0.1x update to avoid kick and energy waste. Saturation back-calculation + yf>0.84 cut to 0 protects 0.9 hard cutoff.",
